             <div class=\"item\">\n   465→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   466→                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/logicoal\" target=\"_blank\">LogiCoal</a>\n   467→                    </div>\n   468→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   469→                        AI multi-agent coding assistant for terminal that handles coding tasks with multi-agent orchestration.\n   470→                    </div>\n   471→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   472→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   473→                        <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n   474→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-29</span>\n   475→                    </div>\n   476→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Multi-agent orchestration for coding tasks\"</div>\n   477→                </div>\n   478→\n   479→                <div class=\"item\">\n   480→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   481→                        <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=46703935\" target=\"_blank\">Architect</a>\n   482→                    </div>\n   483→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   484→                        Terminal built on ghostty-vt terminal emulation for managing multiple AI coding agents. Integrates with Claude Code, Gemini CLI, and Codex agents.\n   485→                    </div>\n   486→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   487→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   488→                        <span class=\"source\">Show HN</span>\n   489→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-25</span>\n   490→                    </div>\n   491→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"A terminal for running multiple AI coding agents\"</div>\n   492→                </div>\n   493→\n   494→                <div class=\"item\">\n   495→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   496→                        <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=46368739\" target=\"_blank\">Superset</a>\n   497→                    </div>\n   498→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   499→                        Open-source terminal designed for managing multiple coding agents (Claude Code, Codex, etc.) in parallel. Can run up to 10 coding agents simultaneously.\n   500→                    </div>\n   501→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   502→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   503→                        <span class=\"source\">Show HN</span>\n   504→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-22</span>\n   505→                    </div>\n   506→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Terminal to run 10 parallel coding agents\"</div>\n   507→                </div>\n   508→\n   509→                <div class=\"item\">\n   510→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   511→                        <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47520220\" target=\"_blank\">Optio</a>\n   512→                    </div>\n   513→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   514→                        Orchestrates AI coding agents in Kubernetes to automate from ticket to PR with CI/CD feedback loops.\n   515→                    </div>\n   516→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   517→                        <span class=\"tag\">workflow agent</span>\n   518→                        <span class=\"source\">Show HN</span>\n   519→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-24</span>\n   520→                    </div>\n   521→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Orchestrates AI coding agents in Kubernetes\"</div>\n   522→                </div>\n   523→\n   524→                <div class=\"item\">\n   525→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   526→                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/struct-2\" target=\"_blank\">Struct</a>\n   527→                    </div>\n   528→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   529→                        AI agent that root-causes engineering alerts using logs, metrics, traces, and code with composable architecture.\n   530→                    </div>\n   531→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   532→                        <span class=\"tag\">workflow agent</span>\n   533→                        <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n   534→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-23</span>\n   535→                    </div>\n   536→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Root-causes engineering alerts\"</div>\n   537→                </div>\n   538→\n   539→                <div class=\"item\">\n   540→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   541→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/plandex-ai/plandex\" target=\"_blank\">Plandex</a>\n   542→                    </div>\n   543→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   544→                        Open-source AI coding agent for large projects - terminal-based tool for planning and executing complex coding tasks.\n   545→                    </div>\n   546→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   547→                        <span class=\"tag\">code agent</span>\n   548→                        <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   549→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-27</span>\n   550→                    </div>\n   551→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Open-source AI coding agent for large projects\"</div>\n   552→                </div>\n   553→\n   554→                <div class=\"item\">\n   555→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   556→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/omnara-ai/omnara\" target=\"_blank\">Omnara</a>\n   557→                    </div>\n   558→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   559→                        AI agent platform that syncs across terminal, web dashboard, and mobile with Claude Code integration - YC S25 startup.\n   560→                    </div>\n   561→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   562→                        <span class=\"tag\">workflow agent</span>\n   563→                        <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   564→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-26</span>\n   565→                    </div>\n   566→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"YC S25 startup\"</div>\n   567→                </div>\n   568→            </section>\n   569→\n   570→            <section class=\"whitelist-updates\">\n   571→                <h2>Product Updates <span class=\"section-count\">(5)</span></h2>\n   572→\n   573→                <div class=\"item\">\n   574→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   575→                        <span class=\"product-name\">GitHub Copilot</span>: Visual Studio April Update\n   576→                    </div>\n   577→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   578→                        April 2026 update centers on agentic workflows: cloud agent sessions launch directly from IDE, custom agents gain user-level support in %USERPROFILE%/.github/agents/, new Debugger agent validates fixes against live runtime behavior, customizable keyboard shortcuts, new chat history panel, and C++ code editing tools now generally available.\n   579→                    </div>\n   580→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   581→                        <span class=\"update-type feature\">Feature</span>\n   582→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-30</span>\n   583→                    </div>\n   584→                    <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-top: 6px;\">\n   585→                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-04-30-github-copilot-in-visual-studio-april-update/\" target=\"_blank\">View Changelog →</a>\n   586→                    </div>\n   587→                </div>\n   588→\n   589→                <div class=\"item\">\n   590→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   591→                        <span class=\"product-name\">Aider</span>: v0.86.0\n   592→                    </div>\n   593→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   594→                        Added support for all GPT-5 models, added support for Grok-4 via xai/grok-4 and openrouter/x-ai/grok-4 model names, added support for gemini-2.5-flash-lite-preview-06-17 model, improved /clear and /undo commands, fixed settings replacement issue, and bumped dependencies to litellm 1.75.0.\n   595→                    </div>\n   596→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   597→                        <span class=\"update-type release\">Release</span>\n   598→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-29</span>\n   599→                    </div>\n   600→                    <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-top: 6px;\">\n   601→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/Aider-AI/aider/releases\" target=\"_blank\">View Release →</a>\n   602→                    </div>\n   603→                </div>\n   604→\n   605→                <div class=\"item\">\n   606→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   607→                        <span class=\"product-name\">Claude Code</span>: Week 17 Updates\n   608→                    </div>\n   609→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   610→                        /ultrareview opens as a research preview, automatic session recaps when returning to terminal, custom color themes for plugins, redesigned web version with sessions sidebar and drag-and-drop layout, Vim visual mode support, hooks can call MCP tools, and performance improvements including 67% faster /resume on large sessions.\n   611→                    </div>\n   612→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   613→                        <span class=\"update-type release\">Release</span>\n   614→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-24</span>\n   615→                    </div>\n   616→                    <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-top: 6px;\">\n   617→                        <a href=\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/whats-new/2026-w17\" target=\"_blank\">View What's New →</a>\n   618→                    </div>\n   619→                </div>\n   620→\n   621→                <div class=\"item\">\n   622→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   623→                        <span class=\"product-name\">Devin</span>: v2.2 Release\n   624→                    </div>\n   625→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   626→                        Desktop support enabled by default for new users, existing users can enable through Settings, enhanced session management indicating 'Action Required' state, minor bug fixes and polish.\n   627→                    </div>\n   628→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   629→                        <span class=\"update-type release\">Release</span>\n   630→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-24</span>\n   631→                    </div>\n   632→                    <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-top: 6px;\">\n   633→                        <a href=\"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/2026\" target=\"_blank\">View Release Notes →</a>\n   634→                    </div>\n   635→                </div>\n   636→\n   637→                <div class=\"item\">\n   638→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   639→                        <span class=\"product-name\">Aider</span>: v0.85.0\n   640→                    </div>\n   641→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   642→                        Added support for new Gemini 2.5 models (pro, flash, preview) with thinking tokens, support for o1-pro and o3-pro models, enhanced thinking tokens configuration, increased max tokens for Deepseek models, new --add-gitignore-files flag, co-authored-by attribution enabled by default, --commit-language option, improved commit message generation, MATLAB and Clojure language support for repository maps.\n   643→                    </div>\n   644→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   645→                        <span class=\"update-type release\">Release</span>\n   646→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-19</span>\n   647→                    </div>\n   648→                    <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-top: 6px;\">\n   649→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/Aider-AI/aider/releases\" target=\"_blank\">View Release →</a>\n   650→                    </div>\n   651→                </div>\n   652→            </section>\n   653→\n   654→            <section class=\"technical-insights\">\n   655→                <h2>Technical Insights <span class=\"section-count\">(0)</span></h2>\n   656→                <div class=\"empty-state\">\n   657→                    No technical insights available for this date.\n   658→                </div>\n   659→            </section>\n   660→        </main>\n   661→\n   662→        <footer>\n   663→            <a href=\"#\">Archives</a>\n   664→            <a href=\"#\">About</a>\n   665→            <a href=\"#\">API</a>\n   666→            <a href=\"#\">Contact</a>\n   667→            <div style=\"margin-top: 8px;\">\n   668→                Generated with <a href=\"https://claude.com/claude-code\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Code</a>\n   669→            </div>\n   670→        </footer>\n   671→    </div>\n   672→</body>\n   673→</html>\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
