   </div>\n                    <div class=\"changelog-link\"><a href=\"https://cursor.sh/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">View Changelog →</a></div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><span class=\"product-name\">Aider</span> v0.86.0</div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">GPT-5 and Grok-4 Support: Added support for all GPT-5 models, Grok-4 via xai/grok-4, gemini-2.5-flash-lite-preview-06-17, improved /clear and /undo commands, litellm 1.75.0.</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type release\">Release</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-29</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"changelog-link\"><a href=\"https://github.com/Aider-AI/aider/releases\" target=\"_blank\">View Release →</a></div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><span class=\"product-name\">Gemini CLI</span> v0.42.0-nightly.20260429</div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">Nightly with transient error policy updates, time-series metric analysis bot, ENOTDIR error messages, ACP stdout pollution prevention, boolean/number casting for env vars, DevTools activity logger improvements, extension-backed MCP client fixes.</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type release\">Release</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-29</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"changelog-link\"><a href=\"https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli/releases\" target=\"_blank\">View Release →</a></div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><span class=\"product-name\">Cursor SDK</span></div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">Introduction of the Cursor SDK for building programmatic agents, enabling developers to create custom agents and automate workflows.</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type feature\">Feature</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-29</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"changelog-link\"><a href=\"https://cursor.com/blog/build-programmatic-agents-with-the-cursor-sdk\" target=\"_blank\">View Blog →</a></div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><span class=\"product-name\">Codex CLI</span> v0.128.0</div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">Major release adding persisted /goal workflows with app-server APIs, model tools, runtime continuation, TUI controls, configurable keymaps, plan-mode nudges, expanded permission profiles, plugin workflows, MCP/plugin improvements.</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type release\">Release</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-27</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"changelog-link\"><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/codex/releases\" target=\"_blank\">View Release →</a></div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><span class=\"product-name\">Cursor</span> v3.2</div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">Multitask, Worktrees, and Multi-root Workspaces: Release with multitask capabilities, git worktrees support, and multi-root workspace functionality for working with multiple codebases simultaneously.</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type release\">Release</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-24</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"changelog-link\"><a href=\"https://cursor.sh/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">View Changelog →</a></div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><span class=\"product-name\">Devin</span> v2.2</div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">Desktop support enabled by default for new users, existing users can enable through Settings, enhanced session management indicating 'Action Required' state, minor bug fixes.</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type release\">Release</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-24</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"changelog-link\"><a href=\"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/2026\" target=\"_blank\">View Release →</a></div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><span class=\"product-name\">Claude Code</span> Week 17</div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">UltraReview Research Preview: /ultrareview opens as research preview, automatic session recaps, custom color themes, redesigned web version, Vim visual mode support, hooks can call MCP tools, 67% faster /resume on large sessions.</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type release\">Release</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-24</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"changelog-link\"><a href=\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/whats-new/2026-w17\" target=\"_blank\">View What's New →</a></div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><span class=\"product-name\">Cursor</span> Security Review</div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">Security enhancements and review updates for the Cursor platform.</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type feature\">Feature</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-30</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"changelog-link\"><a href=\"https://cursor.sh/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">View Changelog →</a></div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><span class=\"product-name\">GitHub Copilot</span> VS April Update</div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">Cloud Agent Integration: Cloud agent sessions launch directly from IDE, custom agents gain user-level support, new Debugger agent validates fixes, customizable keyboard shortcuts, new chat history panel, C++ tools generally available.</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type feature\">Feature</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-30</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"changelog-link\"><a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-04-30-github-copilot-in-visual-studio-april-update/\" target=\"_blank\">View Changelog →</a></div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><span class=\"product-name\">Claude Code</span> v2.1.122</div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">Enhanced Effort Levels: ANTHROPIC_BEDROCK_SERVICE_TIER env var, pasting PR URL into /resume finds session, /mcp shows claude.ai connectors, OpenTelemetry includes numeric attributes and at_mention log events.</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type release\">Release</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-28</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"changelog-link\"><a href=\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">View Changelog →</a></div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><span class=\"product-name\">Claude Code</span> v2.1.121</div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">Performance and Memory: alwaysLoad option for MCP config, claude plugin prune command, type-to-filter search for /skills, fullscreen mode improvements, fixed unbounded memory growth processing images, /resume crash fix.</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type release\">Release</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-28</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"changelog-link\"><a href=\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">View Changelog →</a></div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><span class=\"product-name\">Claude Code</span> v2.1.120</div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">PowerShell Tool: Windows no longer requires Git for Windows, added claude ultrareview subcommand, Skills can reference CLAUDE_EFFORT variable, AI_AGENT environment variable for subprocesses.</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type release\">Release</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-28</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"changelog-link\"><a href=\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">View Changelog →</a></div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><span class=\"product-name\">Claude Code</span> v2.1.119</div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">Config Persistence: /config settings persist to ~/.claude/settings.json, prUrlTemplate setting, CLAUDE_CODE_HIDE_CWD env var, --from-pr accepts GitLab MR and Bitbucket PR URLs, hooks include duration_ms.</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type release\">Release</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-23</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"changelog-link\"><a href=\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">View Changelog →</a></div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><span class=\"product-name\">Claude Code</span> v2.1.118</div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">Custom Themes: Vim visual mode (v) and visual-line mode (V), merged /cost and /stats into /usage, custom themes from /theme, hooks can invoke MCP tools directly, DISABLE_UPDATES env var.</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type release\">Release</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-23</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"changelog-link\"><a href=\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">View Changelog →</a></div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><span class=\"product-name\">Gemini CLI</span> v0.41.0-preview.0</div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">Preview release with secure .env loading, workspace trust, hard-crash fix, shell command validation, Gemma 4 support, real-time voice mode, auto-memory scratchpad persistence, ContextManager integration.</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type release\">Release</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-23</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"changelog-link\"><a href=\"https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli/releases\" target=\"_blank\">View Release →</a></div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><span class=\"product-name\">Windsurf</span> 2.0</div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">Agent Command Center and Devin Integration: Local and cloud agents working together, Devin integration in Windsurf, enhanced collaborative AI capabilities, improved agentic workflows.</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type feature\">Feature</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-15</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"changelog-link\"><a href=\"https://windsurf.com/blog\" target=\"_blank\">View Blog →</a></div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n\n            <section class=\"technical-insights\">\n                <h2>Technical Insights <span class=\"section-count\">(24)</span></h2>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=46570115\" target=\"_blank\">LLM coding workflow going into 2026</a></div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">Hacker News discussion about LLM coding workflows. Users working on multi-step AI pipelines find that LLMs often skip edge cases or take suboptimal paths.</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">discussion</span>\n                        <span class=\"insight-author\">HN Community</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-04</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.02860\" target=\"_blank\">Stabilized Knowledge Distillation</a></div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">Research on stabilized knowledge distillation for cross-language code clone detection, addressing challenges in detecting similar code across different programming languages.</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Paper</span>\n                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Khajezade et al.</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-05</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.02832\" target=\"_blank\">HAAS: Policy-Aware Human-AI Framework</a></div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">Framework for adaptive task allocation between humans and AI systems with policy awareness. Addresses human-AI collaboration and task distribution challenges.</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Paper</span>\n                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Pelechano et al.</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-05</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.02765\" target=\"_blank\">U-Define: LLM Planning Workflows</a></div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">Research on designing user workflows for handling hard and soft constraints in LLM-based planning systems. Explores human-computer interaction challenges with LLM planning agents.</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Paper</span>\n                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Lee et al.</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-05</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.02592\" target=\"_blank\">Foundation-Model-Based Agents in Industrial Automation</a></div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">Comprehensive analysis of foundation-model-based agents in industrial automation, comparing classical agent applications with modern foundation models. 35 pages.</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Paper</span>\n                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Henkel et al.</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-05</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.02572\" target=\"_blank\">Training LLMs for Long-Horizon Tasks</a></div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">Empirical study accepted at ICML 2026 on training LLMs for long-horizon tasks, examining how horizon length affects model performance.</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Paper</span>\n                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Kim et al.</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-05</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.02545\" target=\"_blank\">Strategy-Aware Optimization Modeling</a></div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">Research on strategy-aware optimization modeling using reasoning LLMs. Explores how language models can handle optimization problems with strategic considerations.</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Paper</span>\n                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Zhao et al.</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-05</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.02503\" target=\"_blank\">DataClaw: Agent Benchmark</a></div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">Introduction of DataClaw, a process-oriented agent benchmark designed for exploratory real-world data analysis.</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Paper</span>\n                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Zhang et al.</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-05</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.02475\" target=\"_blank\">Shadow-Loom: Causal Reasoning</a></div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">Shadow-Loom system for causal reasoning over graphical world models of narratives.</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Paper</span>\n                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Wilmot</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-05</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.02452\" target=\"_blank\">How Can Graphs Help LLMs?</a></div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">Position paper examining how graph structures can enhance large language models. Accepted by Frontiers of Computer Science.</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Paper</span>\n                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Wang et al.</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-05</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.02411\" target=\"_blank\">FitText: Evolving Agent Tools</a></div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">Research on FitText, a system for evolving agent tool ecologies through memetic retrieval.</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Paper</span>\n                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Zheng et al.</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-05</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.02398\" target=\"_blank\">The Compliance Trap: AI Metacognition</a></div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">Analysis of how structural constraints and compliance requirements can degrade frontier AI metacognitive capabilities under adversarial pressure.</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Paper</span>\n                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Kumar</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-05</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.02396\" target=\"_blank\">HeavySkill: Agentic Harness</a></div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">HeavySkill framework treating heavy thinking as an inner skill in agentic harness systems. Explores how to effectively harness and control deep reasoning capabilities.</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Paper</span>\n                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Wang et al.</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-05</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.02366\" target=\"_blank\">Compound AI Agent for Grant Discovery</a></div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">Introduction of a compound AI agent designed for conversational grant discovery. Explores multi-agent systems for information discovery tasks.</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Paper</span>\n                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Tang & Kejriwal</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-05</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.02289\" target=\"_blank\">EngiAgent: Multi-Agent Engineering</a></div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">EngiAgent system for fully connected coordination of LLM agents to solve open-ended engineering problems with feasible solutions. Accepted at ICML 2026.</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Paper</span>\n                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Zhou et al.</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-05</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.02269\" target=\"_blank\">Specification Gaming in Reasoning Models</a></div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">Research towards understanding specification gaming in reasoning models. Explores how AI models might game specifications rather than truly solving intended problems.</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Paper</span>\n                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Nishimura-Gasparian et al.</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-05</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Granite 4.1 3B SVG Testing</a></div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">Simon Willison tested IBM's Granite 4.1 family by prompting 'Generate an SVG of a pelican riding a bicycle'. Found results were less interesting than expected.</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Blog</span>\n                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-04</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Zig's Anti-LLM Policy</a></div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">Zig has one of the most stringent anti-LLM policies. Philosophy as 'contributor poker' - they bet on the contributor, not the contents of their first PR.</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Blog</span>\n                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-30</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Codex CLI 0.128.0 /goal Feature</a></div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">OpenAI's Codex CLI version 0.128.0 adds a /goal feature implementing the Ralph loop: set a goal and Codex will keep looping until it evaluates completion.</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Blog</span>\n                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-30</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">UK AI Security Institute Evaluates GPT-5.5</a></div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">The UK's AI Security Institute evaluated GPT-5.5 for finding security vulnerabilities and found it comparable to Claude Mythos.</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Blog</span>\n                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-30</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Detecting LLM Code: 'Digital Smell'</a></div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">Andrew Kelley, creator of Zig: 'The kind of mistakes humans make are fundamentally different than LLM hallucinations...people who come from agentic coding have a certain digital smell.'</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Blog</span>\n                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Andrew Kelley</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-30</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">LLM 0.32a0 Refactor</a></div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">Simon Willison released LLM 0.32a0, an alpha release of his LLM Python library and CLI tool for accessing LLMs.</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Blog</span>\n                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-29</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">OpenAI Codex Base Instructions</a></div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">Instruction from OpenAI Codex: 'Never talk about goblins, gremlins, raccoons, trolls, ogres, pigeons, or other animals unless absolutely and unambiguously relevant.'</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Blog</span>\n                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-28</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">pip 26.1: Lockfiles</a></div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">Python's pip 26.1 adds lockfiles (pip lock writes to pylock.toml) and dependency cooldowns via --uploaded-prior-to option.</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Blog</span>\n                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-28</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Talkie: 13B Vintage Language Model</a></div>\n                    <div class=\"description\">talkie-1930-13b-base, a 13B language model trained on 260B tokens of historical pre-1931 English text, Apache 2.0 licensed.</div>\n                    <div class=\"meta\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Blog</span>\n                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison</span>\n                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-28</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n        </main>\n\n        <footer>\n            <a href=\"#\">Archives</a>\n            <a href=\"#\">About</a>\n            <a href=\"#\">API</a>\n            <a href=\"#\">Contact</a>\n            <div style=\"margin-top: 8px;\">\n                Report generated by <a href=\"https://github.com/anthropics/agent-sdk\" target=\"_blank\">Agent Code Daily</a> - Powered by <a href=\"https://claude.com/claude-code\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Agent SDK</a>\n            </div>\n        </footer>\n    </div>\n</body>\n</html>"
