   <h2>Technical Insights <span class=\"section-count\">(24)</span></h2>\n   707→\n   708→                <div class=\"item\">\n   709→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=46570115\" target=\"_blank\">LLM coding workflow going into 2026</a></div>\n   710→                    <div class=\"description\">Hacker News discussion about LLM coding workflows. Users working on multi-step AI pipelines find that LLMs often skip edge cases or take suboptimal paths.</div>\n   711→                    <div class=\"meta\">\n   712→                        <span class=\"tag\">discussion</span>\n   713→                        <span class=\"insight-author\">HN Community</span>\n   714→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-04</span>\n   715→                    </div>\n   716→                </div>\n   717→\n   718→                <div class=\"item\">\n   719→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.02860\" target=\"_blank\">Stabilized Knowledge Distillation</a></div>\n   720→                    <div class=\"description\">Research on stabilized knowledge distillation for cross-language code clone detection, addressing challenges in detecting similar code across different programming languages.</div>\n   721→                    <div class=\"meta\">\n   722→                        <span class=\"tag\">Paper</span>\n   723→                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Khajezade et al.</span>\n   724→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-05</span>\n   725→                    </div>\n   726→                </div>\n   727→\n   728→                <div class=\"item\">\n   729→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.02832\" target=\"_blank\">HAAS: Policy-Aware Human-AI Framework</a></div>\n   730→                    <div class=\"description\">Framework for adaptive task allocation between humans and AI systems with policy awareness. Addresses human-AI collaboration and task distribution challenges.</div>\n   731→                    <div class=\"meta\">\n   732→                        <span class=\"tag\">Paper</span>\n   733→                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Pelechano et al.</span>\n   734→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-05</span>\n   735→                    </div>\n   736→                </div>\n   737→\n   738→                <div class=\"item\">\n   739→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.02765\" target=\"_blank\">U-Define: LLM Planning Workflows</a></div>\n   740→                    <div class=\"description\">Research on designing user workflows for handling hard and soft constraints in LLM-based planning systems. Explores human-computer interaction challenges with LLM planning agents.</div>\n   741→                    <div class=\"meta\">\n   742→                        <span class=\"tag\">Paper</span>\n   743→                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Lee et al.</span>\n   744→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-05</span>\n   745→                    </div>\n   746→                </div>\n   747→\n   748→                <div class=\"item\">\n   749→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.02592\" target=\"_blank\">Foundation-Model-Based Agents in Industrial Automation</a></div>\n   750→                    <div class=\"description\">Comprehensive analysis of foundation-model-based agents in industrial automation, comparing classical agent applications with modern foundation models. 35 pages.</div>\n   751→                    <div class=\"meta\">\n   752→                        <span class=\"tag\">Paper</span>\n   753→                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Henkel et al.</span>\n   754→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-05</span>\n   755→                    </div>\n   756→                </div>\n   757→\n   758→                <div class=\"item\">\n   759→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.02572\" target=\"_blank\">Training LLMs for Long-Horizon Tasks</a></div>\n   760→                    <div class=\"description\">Empirical study accepted at ICML 2026 on training LLMs for long-horizon tasks, examining how horizon length affects model performance.</div>\n   761→                    <div class=\"meta\">\n   762→                        <span class=\"tag\">Paper</span>\n   763→                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Kim et al.</span>\n   764→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-05</span>\n   765→                    </div>\n   766→                </div>\n   767→\n   768→                <div class=\"item\">\n   769→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.02545\" target=\"_blank\">Strategy-Aware Optimization Modeling</a></div>\n   770→                    <div class=\"description\">Research on strategy-aware optimization modeling using reasoning LLMs. Explores how language models can handle optimization problems with strategic considerations.</div>\n   771→                    <div class=\"meta\">\n   772→                        <span class=\"tag\">Paper</span>\n   773→                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Zhao et al.</span>\n   774→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-05</span>\n   775→                    </div>\n   776→                </div>\n   777→\n   778→                <div class=\"item\">\n   779→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.02503\" target=\"_blank\">DataClaw: Agent Benchmark</a></div>\n   780→                    <div class=\"description\">Introduction of DataClaw, a process-oriented agent benchmark designed for exploratory real-world data analysis.</div>\n   781→                    <div class=\"meta\">\n   782→                        <span class=\"tag\">Paper</span>\n   783→                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Zhang et al.</span>\n   784→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-05</span>\n   785→                    </div>\n   786→                </div>\n   787→\n   788→                <div class=\"item\">\n   789→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.02475\" target=\"_blank\">Shadow-Loom: Causal Reasoning</a></div>\n   790→                    <div class=\"description\">Shadow-Loom system for causal reasoning over graphical world models of narratives.</div>\n   791→                    <div class=\"meta\">\n   792→                        <span class=\"tag\">Paper</span>\n   793→                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Wilmot</span>\n   794→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-05</span>\n   795→                    </div>\n   796→                </div>\n   797→\n   798→                <div class=\"item\">\n   799→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.02452\" target=\"_blank\">How Can Graphs Help LLMs?</a></div>\n   800→                    <div class=\"description\">Position paper examining how graph structures can enhance large language models. Accepted by Frontiers of Computer Science.</div>\n   801→                    <div class=\"meta\">\n   802→                        <span class=\"tag\">Paper</span>\n   803→                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Wang et al.</span>\n   804→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-05</span>\n   805→                    </div>\n   806→                </div>\n   807→\n   808→                <div class=\"item\">\n   809→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.02411\" target=\"_blank\">FitText: Evolving Agent Tools</a></div>\n   810→                    <div class=\"description\">Research on FitText, a system for evolving agent tool ecologies through memetic retrieval.</div>\n   811→                    <div class=\"meta\">\n   812→                        <span class=\"tag\">Paper</span>\n   813→                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Zheng et al.</span>\n   814→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-05</span>\n   815→                    </div>\n   816→                </div>\n   817→\n   818→                <div class=\"item\">\n   819→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.02398\" target=\"_blank\">The Compliance Trap: AI Metacognition</a></div>\n   820→                    <div class=\"description\">Analysis of how structural constraints and compliance requirements can degrade frontier AI metacognitive capabilities under adversarial pressure.</div>\n   821→                    <div class=\"meta\">\n   822→                        <span class=\"tag\">Paper</span>\n   823→                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Kumar</span>\n   824→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-05</span>\n   825→                    </div>\n   826→                </div>\n   827→\n   828→                <div class=\"item\">\n   829→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.02396\" target=\"_blank\">HeavySkill: Agentic Harness</a></div>\n   830→                    <div class=\"description\">HeavySkill framework treating heavy thinking as an inner skill in agentic harness systems. Explores how to effectively harness and control deep reasoning capabilities.</div>\n   831→                    <div class=\"meta\">\n   832→                        <span class=\"tag\">Paper</span>\n   833→                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Wang et al.</span>\n   834→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-05</span>\n   835→                    </div>\n   836→                </div>\n   837→\n   838→                <div class=\"item\">\n   839→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.02366\" target=\"_blank\">Compound AI Agent for Grant Discovery</a></div>\n   840→                    <div class=\"description\">Introduction of a compound AI agent designed for conversational grant discovery. Explores multi-agent systems for information discovery tasks.</div>\n   841→                    <div class=\"meta\">\n   842→                        <span class=\"tag\">Paper</span>\n   843→                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Tang & Kejriwal</span>\n   844→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-05</span>\n   845→                    </div>\n   846→                </div>\n   847→\n   848→                <div class=\"item\">\n   849→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.02289\" target=\"_blank\">EngiAgent: Multi-Agent Engineering</a></div>\n   850→                    <div class=\"description\">EngiAgent system for fully connected coordination of LLM agents to solve open-ended engineering problems with feasible solutions. Accepted at ICML 2026.</div>\n   851→                    <div class=\"meta\">\n   852→                        <span class=\"tag\">Paper</span>\n   853→                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Zhou et al.</span>\n   854→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-05</span>\n   855→                    </div>\n   856→                </div>\n   857→\n   858→                <div class=\"item\">\n   859→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.02269\" target=\"_blank\">Specification Gaming in Reasoning Models</a></div>\n   860→                    <div class=\"description\">Research towards understanding specification gaming in reasoning models. Explores how AI models might game specifications rather than truly solving intended problems.</div>\n   861→                    <div class=\"meta\">\n   862→                        <span class=\"tag\">Paper</span>\n   863→                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Nishimura-Gasparian et al.</span>\n   864→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-05</span>\n   865→                    </div>\n   866→                </div>\n   867→\n   868→                <div class=\"item\">\n   869→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Granite 4.1 3B SVG Testing</a></div>\n   870→                    <div class=\"description\">Simon Willison tested IBM's Granite 4.1 family by prompting 'Generate an SVG of a pelican riding a bicycle'. Found results were less interesting than expected.</div>\n   871→                    <div class=\"meta\">\n   872→                        <span class=\"tag\">Blog</span>\n   873→                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison</span>\n   874→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-04</span>\n   875→                    </div>\n   876→                </div>\n   877→\n   878→                <div class=\"item\">\n   879→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Zig's Anti-LLM Policy</a></div>\n   880→                    <div class=\"description\">Zig has one of the most stringent anti-LLM policies. Philosophy as 'contributor poker' - they bet on the contributor, not the contents of their first PR.</div>\n   881→                    <div class=\"meta\">\n   882→                        <span class=\"tag\">Blog</span>\n   883→                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison</span>\n   884→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-30</span>\n   885→                    </div>\n   886→                </div>\n   887→\n   888→                <div class=\"item\">\n   889→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Codex CLI 0.128.0 /goal Feature</a></div>\n   890→                    <div class=\"description\">OpenAI's Codex CLI version 0.128.0 adds a /goal feature implementing the Ralph loop: set a goal and Codex will keep looping until it evaluates completion.</div>\n   891→                    <div class=\"meta\">\n   892→                        <span class=\"tag\">Blog</span>\n   893→                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison</span>\n   894→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-30</span>\n   895→                    </div>\n   896→                </div>\n   897→\n   898→                <div class=\"item\">\n   899→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">UK AI Security Institute Evaluates GPT-5.5</a></div>\n   900→                    <div class=\"description\">The UK's AI Security Institute evaluated GPT-5.5 for finding security vulnerabilities and found it comparable to Claude Mythos.</div>\n   901→                    <div class=\"meta\">\n   902→                        <span class=\"tag\">Blog</span>\n   903→                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison</span>\n   904→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-30</span>\n   905→                    </div>\n   906→                </div>\n   907→\n   908→                <div class=\"item\">\n   909→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Detecting LLM Code: 'Digital Smell'</a></div>\n   910→                    <div class=\"description\">Andrew Kelley, creator of Zig: 'The kind of mistakes humans make are fundamentally different than LLM hallucinations...people who come from agentic coding have a certain digital smell.'</div>\n   911→                    <div class=\"meta\">\n   912→                        <span class=\"tag\">Blog</span>\n   913→                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Andrew Kelley</span>\n   914→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-30</span>\n   915→                    </div>\n   916→                </div>\n   917→\n   918→                <div class=\"item\">\n   919→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">LLM 0.32a0 Refactor</a></div>\n   920→                    <div class=\"description\">Simon Willison released LLM 0.32a0, an alpha release of his LLM Python library and CLI tool for accessing LLMs.</div>\n   921→                    <div class=\"meta\">\n   922→                        <span class=\"tag\">Blog</span>\n   923→                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison</span>\n   924→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-29</span>\n   925→                    </div>\n   926→                </div>\n   927→\n   928→                <div class=\"item\">\n   929→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">OpenAI Codex Base Instructions</a></div>\n   930→                    <div class=\"description\">Instruction from OpenAI Codex: 'Never talk about goblins, gremlins, raccoons, trolls, ogres, pigeons, or other animals unless absolutely and unambiguously relevant.'</div>\n   931→                    <div class=\"meta\">\n   932→                        <span class=\"tag\">Blog</span>\n   933→                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison</span>\n   934→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-28</span>\n   935→                    </div>\n   936→                </div>\n   937→\n   938→                <div class=\"item\">\n   939→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">pip 26.1: Lockfiles</a></div>\n   940→                    <div class=\"description\">Python's pip 26.1 adds lockfiles (pip lock writes to pylock.toml) and dependency cooldowns via --uploaded-prior-to option.</div>\n   941→                    <div class=\"meta\">\n   942→                        <span class=\"tag\">Blog</span>\n   943→                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison</span>\n   944→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-28</span>\n   945→                    </div>\n   946→                </div>\n   947→\n   948→                <div class=\"item\">\n   949→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Talkie: 13B Vintage Language Model</a></div>\n   950→                    <div class=\"description\">talkie-1930-13b-base, a 13B language model trained on 260B tokens of historical pre-1931 English text, Apache 2.0 licensed.</div>\n   951→                    <div class=\"meta\">\n   952→                        <span class=\"tag\">Blog</span>\n   953→                        <span class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison</span>\n   954→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-04-28</span>\n   955→                    </div>\n   956→                </div>\n   957→            </section>\n   958→        </main>\n   959→\n   960→        <footer>\n   961→            <a href=\"#\">Archives</a>\n   962→            <a href=\"#\">About</a>\n   963→            <a href=\"#\">API</a>\n   964→            <a href=\"#\">Contact</a>\n   965→            <div style=\"margin-top: 8px;\">\n   966→                Report generated by <a href=\"https://github.com/anthropics/agent-sdk\" target=\"_blank\">Agent Code Daily</a> - Powered by <a href=\"https://claude.com/claude-code\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Agent SDK</a>\n   967→            </div>\n   968→        </footer>\n   969→    </div>\n   970→</body>\n   971→</html>"
